"t": "οὗτος", "o": 19, "k": "ou(=tos"}, {"t": "ὁ", "o": 25, "k": "o("}, {"t": "τόπος", "o": 27, "k": "to/pos"}, {"t": "ἐν", "o": 34, "k": "e)n"}, {"t": "ᾧ", "o": 37, "k": "w(=|"}, {"t": "τὸ", "o": 39, "k": "to/"}, {"t": "γλίσχρον", "o": 42, "k": "gli/sxron"}, {"t": "καὶ", "o": 51, "k": "kai/"}]}, {"n": 33, "text": "κολλῶδες, ὥστε ἔργον μεταστῆσαι, τῇ δὲ κοιλίᾳ ἐγγύς; ἢ", "tokens": [{"t": "κολλῶδες", "o": 0, "k": "kollw=des"}, {"t": "ὥστε", "o": 10, "k": "w(/ste"}, {"t": "ἔργον", "o": 15, "k": "e)/rgon"}, {"t": "μεταστῆσαι", "o": 21, "k": "metasth=sai"}, {"t": "τῇ", "o": 33, "k": "th=|"}, {"t": "δὲ", "o": 36, "k": "de/"}, {"t": "κοιλίᾳ", "o": 39, "k": "koili/a|"}, {"t": "ἐγγύς", "o": 46, "k": "e)ggu/s"}, {"t": "ἢ", "o": 53, "k": "h)/"}]}, {"n": 34, "text": "γὰρ ἐν ταύτῃ γίνεται ἢ πλησίον· διὸ καὶ δυσεξάγωγος", "tokens": [{"t": "γὰρ", "o": 0, "k": "ga/r"}, {"t": "ἐν", "o": 4, "k": "e)n"}, {"t": "ταύτῃ", "o": 7, "k": "tau/th|"}, {"t": "γίνεται", "o": 13, "k": "gi/netai"}, {"t": "ἢ", "o": 21, "k": "h)/"}, {"t": "πλησίον", "o": 23, "k": "plhsi/on"}, {"t": "διὸ", "o": 32, "k": "dio/"}, {"t": "καὶ", "o": 36, "k": "kai/"}, {"t": "δυσεξάγωγος", "o": 40, "k": "duseca/gwgos"}]}, {"n": 35, "text": "ἄλλως.", "tokens": [{"t": "ἄλλως", "o": 0, "k": "a)/llws"}]}, {"n": 36, "text": "Διὰ τί αἱ τρίψεις σαρκοῦσιν; ἢ ὅτι αὐξητικώτατον", "tokens": [{"t": "Διὰ", "o": 0, "k": "dia/"}, {"t": "τί", "o": 4, "k": "ti/"}, {"t": "αἱ", "o": 7, "k": "ai("}, {"t": "τρίψεις", "o": 10, "k": "tri/yeis"}, {"t": "σαρκοῦσιν", "o": 18, "k": "sarkou=sin"}, {"t": "ἢ", "o": 29, "k": "h)/"}, {"t": "ὅτι", "o": 31, "k": "o(/ti"}, {"t": "αὐξητικώτατον", "o": 35, "k": "au)chtikw/taton"}]}, {"n": 37, "text": "τῶν ἐν τῷ σώματι τὸ θερμόν ἐστιν; τοῦ μὲν γὰρ ἐνυπάρχοντος", "joined": true, "tokens": [{"t": "τῶν", "o": 0, "k": "tw=n"}, {"t": "ἐν", "o": 4, "k": "e)n"}, {"t": "τῷ", "o": 7, "k": "tw=|"}, {"t": "σώματι", "o": 10, "k": "sw/mati"}, {"t": "τὸ", "o": 17, "k": "to/"}, {"t": "θερμόν", "o": 20, "k": "qermo/n"}, {"t": "ἐστιν", "o": 27, "k": "e)stin"}, {"t": "τοῦ", "o": 34, "k": "tou="}, {"t": "μὲν", "o": 38, "k": "me/n"}, {"t": "γὰρ", "o": 42, "k": "ga/r"}, {"t": "ἐνυπάρχοντος", "o": 46, "k": "e)nupa/rxontos"}]}, {"n": 38, "text": "μείζους οἱ ὄγκοι γίνονται διὰ τὸ ἀεὶ αὐτὸ ἐν κινήσει", "joined": true, "tokens": [{"t": "μείζους", "o": 0, "k": "mei/zous"}, {"t": "οἱ", "o": 8, "k": "oi("}, {"t": "ὄγκοι", "o": 11, "k": "o)/gkoi"}, {"t": "γίνονται", "o": 17, "k": "gi/nontai"}, {"t": "διὰ", "o": 26, "k": "dia/"}, {"t": "τὸ", "o": 30, "k": "to/"}, {"t": "ἀεὶ", "o": 33, "k": "a)ei/"}, {"t": "αὐτὸ", "o": 37, "k": "au)to/"}, {"t": "ἐν", "o": 42, "k": "e)n"}, {"t": "κινήσει", "o": 45, "k": "kinh/sei"}]}, {"n": 39, "text": "εἶναι καὶ εἰς τὸ ἄνω φέρεσθαι καὶ πνευματοῦν τὰ ἐν", "tokens": [{"t": "εἶναι", "o": 0, "k": "ei)=nai"}, {"t": "καὶ", "o": 6, "k": "kai/"}, {"t": "εἰς", "o": 10, "k": "ei)s"}, {"t": "τὸ", "o": 14, "k": "to/"}, {"t": "ἄνω", "o": 17, "k": "a)/nw"}, {"t": "φέρεσθαι", "o": 21, "k": "fe/resqai"}, {"t": "καὶ", "o": 30, "k": "kai/"}, {"t": "πνευματοῦν", "o": 34, "k": "pneumatou=n"}, {"t": "τὰ", "o": 45, "k": "ta/"}, {"t": "ἐν", "o": 48, "k": "e)n"}]}], "english": {"text": "Why is it that, though the body is in a state of continual flux, and effluvia are given off from the excrements, the body is only lightened if it perspires? Is it because the excretion in the form of effluvia is too little (for when liquid is transformed into air, much air is formed out of little liquid)? For what is excreted is more, which accounts for the excretion taking longer to begin. And what is the reason of this? Is it because its exit takes place through smaller pores? For the viscous and the adhesive matter is expelled with the moisture because it mingles with it, but it cannot be expelled with the breath; and it is this thick matter in particular which causes pain. Therefore also vomiting lightens the body more than sweating, because that which is vomited, being thicker and more substantial, carries away this viscous matter with it. Or is there a further reason, namely, that the region in which the viscous and the adhesive matter is, is situated at a distance in relation to the flesh (and so it is difficult to make it change its position), but near to the stomach? For it is engendered either in or close to it; and therefore it is difficult to get rid of it in any other way. Why is it that friction produces flesh? Is it because heat has great power to increase what is in the body? For the bulk of what already exists in it becomes greater if the body is in continual motion and if our internal humours are carried upwards and vaporized, and this occurs as", "notes": [], "markers": [{"kind": "section", "n": "1", "offset": 0}, {"kind": "section", "n": "2", "offset": 394}, {"kind": "section", "n": "3", "offset": 1205}], "bekker": [{"n": 20, "offset": 0, "real": true}, {"n": 25, "offset": 284, "real": true}, {"n": 30, "offset": 738, "real": true}, {"n": 35, "offset": 1093, "real": true}]}}, {"id": "37:966a", "column": "966a", "chapterStarts": [{"chapter": "4", "beforeLine": 35, "wordIndex": 0, "engOffset": 2418, "bekker": "966a35–39"}], "greek": [{"n": 1, "text": "ἡμῖν ὑγρά, ὃ ἐν τῇ τρίψει γίνεται· ἐκλείποντος δὲ φθίνει", "tokens": [{"t": "ἡμῖν", "o": 0, "k": "h(mi=n"}, {"t": "ὑγρά", "o": 5, "k": "u(gra/"}, {"t": "ὃ", "o": 11, "k": "o(/"}, {"t": "ἐν", "o": 13, "k": "e)n"}, {"t": "τῇ", "o": 16, "k": "th=|"}, {"t": "τρίψει", "o": 19, "k": "tri/yei"}, {"t": "γίνεται", "o": 26, "k": "gi/netai"}, {"t": "ἐκλείποντος", "o": 35, "k": "e)klei/pontos"}, {"t": "δὲ", "o": 47, "k": "de/"}, {"t": "φθίνει", "o": 50, "k": "fqi/nei"}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "καὶ ἐλαττοῦται τὸ σῶμα. ἢ ὅτι ὀγκοτέρα τῆς τροφῆς γίνεται", "joined": true, "tokens": [{"t": "καὶ", "o": 0, "k": "kai/"}, {"t": "ἐλαττοῦται", "o": 4, "k": "e)lattou=tai"}, {"t": "τὸ", "o": 15, "k": "to/"}, {"t": "σῶμα", "o": 18, "k": "sw=ma"}, {"t": "ἢ", "o": 24, "k": "h)/"}, {"t": "ὅτι", "o": 26, "k": "o(/ti"}, {"t": "ὀγκοτέρα", 